        "## Environment and Reproducibility\n",
        "\n",
        "This cell installs the numerical, quantum-simulation, and machine-learning dependencies required by the notebook. The experiment is intentionally reproducible: later cells use fixed seeds for dataset generation, parameter initialization, contextual error injection, and strict single-shot measurement.\n",
        "\n",
        "The quantum experiment must distinguish three objects:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "E_l^{\\mathrm{ideal}},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "M_l^{(1)},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "R_l=M_l^{(1)}-E_l^{\\mathrm{ideal}},\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where $E_l^{\\mathrm{ideal}}$ is the independently propagated clean contextual expectation, $M_l^{(1)}$ is the strict one-shot measurement, and $R_l$ is the residual used by the deterministic reference-projection audit."
