        "## Global Experimental Configuration\n",
        "\n",
        "The experiment uses a 15-qubit, 15-layer QFT-aware variational circuit. A fixed heterogeneous coherent error map is generated once for every layer and qubit:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "E_{l,q}\n",
        "=\n",
        "R_Z(\\epsilon^Z_{l,q})\n",
        "R_Y(\\epsilon^Y_{l,q})\n",
        "R_X(\\epsilon^X_{l,q}).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The injected error is placed **inside circuit depth**, so an error introduced at layer $l$ changes the state entering layers $l+1,\\ldots,L$. The clean reference is propagated independently through the same legitimate circuit prefix.\n",
        "\n",
        "The dataset is deliberately small and randomly generated. This is a controlled demonstration rather than a benchmark intended to maximize held-out predictive performance.\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Random generated bir dataset olması ve kasıtlı olarak küçük bir veriseti olarak generate edilmesindeki maksat, modelin kısıtlı feature space ihtiva eden verisetinde dahi yüksek öğrenme metriklerine ulaşmayı başarabildiğini göstererek, çerçevenin hatayı başarılı bir şekilde ayıkladığını göstermektir.**\n",
        "\n",
        "In English: the purpose of deliberately generating a small random dataset is to test whether the model can still attain strong learning metrics in a restricted feature space while the contextual error is separated from legitimate quantum evolution.\n",
        "\n",
        "Therefore, a train/test gap must be interpreted in the context of the **small, generated dataset and limited feature space**. The objective of this notebook is **not to obtain the highest possible test score**. High learning metrics are supporting evidence that the representation remains learnable under the correction framework; the direct evidence for correction itself comes from residual decomposition, leakage boundaries, and reference-recovery metrics."
      ]
