        "The Hamiltonian-style audit combines these channels as\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "H_l\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\sum_q\n",
        "\\left(\n",
        "w_X\\langle X_q\\rangle+\n",
        "w_Y\\langle Y_q\\rangle+\n",
        "w_Z\\langle Z_q\\rangle\n",
        "\\right).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Keeping all three axes allows the correction analysis to detect contextual displacement that would be hidden by a single-axis measurement."
