        "A train/test difference is therefore expected to be more volatile than it would be for a large representative dataset. With only a limited generated sample, the held-out partition has higher sampling uncertainty and covers the feature space less completely.\n",
        "\n",
        "Most importantly, **the goal is not a maximum test score**. Strong learning metrics are included because successful learning under these constrained conditions supports the conclusion that the correction process has not destroyed the useful task representation."
