        "## Strict Single-Shot Residual, Contextual Reference, and Leakage Boundary\n",
        "\n",
        "This is the central correction/audit cell.\n",
        "\n",
        "At every relevant layer, the clean contextual expectation is independently propagated. The strict single-shot measurement is compared with that reference:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "R_l\n",
        "=\n",
        "M_l^{(1)}-E_l^{\\mathrm{ideal}}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The deterministic reference projection is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "M_l^{\\mathrm{corr}}\n",
        "=\n",
        "M_l^{(1)}-R_l\n",
        "=\n",
        "E_l^{\\mathrm{ideal}}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The correction function does **not** construct its residual from the injected `CONTEXT_RX_ERROR`, `CONTEXT_RY_ERROR`, `CONTEXT_RZ_ERROR`, the random-noise seed, or the exact noisy expectation. Those quantities may exist in the notebook for controlled evaluator-side validation, but they are not inputs to the correction reference.\n",
        "\n",
        "The correction percentage is calculated as\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "C\n",
        "=\n",
        "100\\left(\n",
        "1-\n",
        "\\frac{\n",
        "\\operatorname{MAE}(M^{\\mathrm{corr}},E^{\\mathrm{ideal}})\n",
        "}{\n",
        "\\operatorname{MAE}(M^{(1)},E^{\\mathrm{ideal}})\n",
        "}\n",
        "\\right).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Because this is a deterministic reference projection, exact recovery of the supplied reference is algebraically expected up to numerical precision. This percentage must therefore be described as **contextual-reference recovery**, not as blind inference of an unknown physical hardware error."
      ]
    },
